  "text": "Katie Wright, DVM, DACVIM, MedVet Salt Lake City\nFor Pet Parents\nFor Veterinarians\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFind a Clinic\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nFind a Clinic\nReferral Partner Login\nRefer a Patient\nLocations\nFind A Doctor\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSocial Work\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nReferral Partner Resources\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFor Pet Parents\nFind Care\nSpecialties\nResources\nAbout\nFor Veterinarians\nSpecialties\nVet Resources\nAbout\nMedVet Training Programs\nWork at MedVet\nEmergency Care\nRefer a Patient\nFind a Doctor\nKatie Wright\nKatie Wright, DVM, DACVIM\nBoard-Certified Veterinary Oncologist\nKatie Wright, DVM, Diplomate, ACVIM, is a\nBoard-Certified Veterinary Oncologist\nat\nMedVet Salt Lake City\n.\nDr. Wright earned a Bachelor of science degree in Zoology with a minor in animal science and environmental science from North Carolina State University. She then attended the Oklahoma State University College of Veterinary Medicine where she earned a Doctor of Veterinary Medicine degree. Following earning her veterinary degree, Dr. Wright completed a small animal rotating internship at the Cornell University College of Veterinary Medicine. Additionally, she completed a medical oncology residency at the world-renowned Animal Medical Center.\nDr. Katie Wright is experienced in all aspects of small animal oncology with specific areas of interest in lymphoproliferative disorders (leukemia and lymphoma), hemangiosarcoma, clinical research trials, diagnostic imaging, comparative oncology, and One Health. Her favorite part of practicing medicine is helping families understand the cancer diagnosis their pet is facing so that together, they can come up with the best treatment plan.\nWhen not caring for her patients, you can find Dr. Wright rock climbing, skiing, hiking, traveling, and entertaining her two cats, Toast (Maine Coon) and Possum (domestic short hair).\nEducation & Training\nBachelor of Science:\nNorth Carolina State University\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine:\nOklahoma State University College of Veterinary Medicine\nInternship (Rotating Small Animal Medicine and Surgery):\nCornell University\nResidency (Medical Oncology):\nAnimal Medical Center\nSpecializations\nBoard Certification:\nDiplomate of the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (Medical Oncology)\nAssociations\nAmerican Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA)\nVeterinary Cancer Society (VCS)\nVeterinary Society of Surgical Oncology (VSSO)\nAmerican College of Veterinary Internal Medicine (ACVIM)\nSpecialties\nMedical Oncology\nServicing Locations\nMedVet Salt Lake City\nMeet The Specialist\nIn our “Meet the Specialist” series, we are taking you behind the scenes to get to know our specialists better and to show you why we love our team members so much! Meet Dr. Katie Wright, Veterinary Oncologist at MedVet Salt Lake City.\nMeet The Specialist\nIn our “Meet the Specialist” series, we are taking you behind the scenes to get to 